  "narrative": {
    "intro": "The state of Iowa recorded $1.5B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense obligated $949M, making the Department of Defense the largest buying agency in the state this fiscal year to date. The federal award count in Iowa reached 20,098, with an average award size of $73.7K. Obligations fell 59.0% year over year. The FY26 total contrasts with prior full fiscal years: FY25 totaled $3.6B, FY24 totaled $3B, FY23 totaled $3.4B, FY22 totaled $2.7B, and FY21 totaled $2.5B. Other large buying agencies in FY2026 to date include the Department of the Treasury with $175M and the Department of Agriculture with $106M. Industry concentration is notable: Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing accounted for $289M and Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying accounted for $116M. ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. and DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC are the top vendors, with ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. receiving $315M and DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC receiving $277M in obligations so far this fiscal year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What explains the year-over-year decline in obligations?",
        "body": "Obligations fell 59.0% year over year in FY2026 to date. The FY26 obligations of $1.5B are lower than FY25 obligations of $3.6B and previous full-year totals. The Department of Defense remained the largest buyer with $949M, but overall statewide obligations are substantially below the prior fiscal-year totals. The FY2026 totals are partial, fiscal year to date."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies, industries, and vendors dominate Iowa contracting this year to date?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense is the largest buying agency with $949M, followed by the Department of the Treasury with $175M and the Department of Agriculture with $106M. Other Communications Equipment Manufacturing leads industries with $289M, and Copper Rolling, Drawing, Extruding, and Alloying accounted for $116M. ROCKWELL COLLINS, INC. and DATA LINK SOLUTIONS LLC are the top vendors with $315M and $277M respectively."
      }
    ]
  },
